Currently: "invalid implicit conversion from 'signed int' to 'struct
tup'" while converting pf's constructor (the tup<B...> member's
mem-initializer under the partial specialization's two live packs), then
no body for the constructor and assertion FAILURE.  Runtime-verified
with g++ and clang++.  This is the remaining blocker of
cpp20_ranges_pipe_invoke_drop (round-55 diagnosis).
Round-56 progress: the [temp.variadic]/5 half is FIXED (the bare
`b...` mem-init argument now resolves to the materialised parameters).
Remaining: initializing the pack-typed member `tup<B...> bound_` from
that single argument needs C++20 PARENTHESIZED AGGREGATE initialization
for a MEMBER ([dcl.init.general]/16.6.2.2) -- the existing routes cover
